-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",7,{
[193]="7002724B\n1\tAid Andreg with Eyes in the Forest\tAmlan told you to summon Andreg and accompany him to the Rohirrim scout-camp to meet with Saeradan. If you become separated from Andreg, you may summon him using the bird-whistle Amlan gave you.\n2\tTalk to Andreg\tAndreg has accompanied you for some distance. Now the time has come to part ways. You should speak with Andreg. Advancing this quest will no longer allow you to summon Andreg and will cancel any quests bestowed by him that are currently underway.\n3\tTalk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tSaeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp. Andreg told you to continue on to the Rohirrim scout-camp and let Saeradan know that he is scouting the wood to the south and east.\n",
[194]="7002C953\n1\tAid Andreg with Eyes in the Forest\tAmlan told you to summon Andreg and accompany him to the Rohirrim scout-camp to meet with Saeradan. If you become separated from Andreg, you may summon him using the bird-whistle Amlan gave you.\n2\tTalk to Andreg\tAndreg has accompanied you for some distance. Now the time has come to part ways. You should speak with Andreg. Advancing this quest will no longer allow you to summon Andreg.\n3\tTalk to Saeradan at the Rohirrim scout-camp\tSaeradan is at the Rohirrim scout-camp. Andreg told you to continue on to the Rohirrim scout-camp and let Saeradan know that he is scouting the wood to the south and east.\n",
[195]="70015E16\n1\tHelp Ruidhriel\030Help Limlaer\tRuidhriel is encamped near the Burnt Tor, north-west of Echad Dúnann. Limlaer may be found along the road, south-west of Echad Dúnann. Rinneldor has asked you to once again speak with Ruidhriel and Limlaer to learn what must be done to confuse the Company's trail.\n2\tTalk to Rinneldor at Echad Dúnann\tRinneldor is at Echad Dúnann, south-east of the Burnt Tor and north-east of Limlaer's post. You should return to Rinneldor with news of your successes.\n",
[196]="7000875D\n1\tReturn to Taskmaster Gukthor at Dâr-gazag\030Collect brittleleaf-seeds (total: 5)\tThe rat-folk living south of Dâr-gazag along the river grow a plant that can be crushed to make a tasty spice. Taskmaster Gukthor waits for you to return with the brittle-leaf seeds.\n",
[197]="700571BF\n1\tGather honey (total: 10)\030Defeat frenzied bees (total: 6)\tHoney can be found at the forest's edge in the eastern reaches of the Floodfells. You should gather honey for Limlók.\n2\tPlace the honey in jars at Limlók (total: 2)\tHoney jars can be found in Limlók. You should fill up the empty honey jars.\n",
[198]="70007EF6\n1\tDestroy Skorgrím's Bloom plants (total: 6)\tSkorgrím's Bloom can be found flowering along the path leading to Mirkstone Tunnels, north-west of Frerin's Court. Destroy the poisonous blossoms, lest they spread down the mountainside.\n2\tTalk to Erynwen\tErynwen is found at the centre of Frerin's Court. You destroyed some of the Skorgrím's Bloom plants, as Erynwen asked.\n",
[199]="70027B66\n1\tFind a source of fresh water in the mine\tThere must be a source of fresh water somewhere in the Orc-mines. Edhere has asked you to find a source of fresh water for the miners who are dying of thirst.\n2\tBring water to the exhausted miners (total: 6)\tThe exhausted miners can be found in the Orc-mines. You should bring the fresh water to the exhausted miners as Edhere requested.\n3\tTalk to Edhere in the Orc-mines\tEdhere is in the Orc-mines. You should return to Edhere and let him know that you have found fresh water.\n",
[200]="70050E1C\n1\tDefeat the Gundabad Reaver\tA deadly Gundabad Reaver roams the west, near Rushgate.\n2\tDefeat the Gundabad Reaver\tA deadly Gundabad Reaver roams the west, near Rushgate.\n3\tCompleted\tA deadly Gundabad Reaver roams the west, near Rushgate.\n",
[201]="7000005A\n1\tSpeak with Pengail\tThe Forsaken Inn is south-west of the goblin encampment. Pengail has asked you to help him escape the goblins and take him to The Forsaken Inn.\n2\tTalk to Anlaf the Forlorn\tAnlaf the Forlorn is at The Forsaken Inn. After you helped him escape and find his father's sword, Pengail told you that Anlaf the Forlorn has the valuables that he left in his room. He told you to let Anlaf know that he is free and that he offered you a reward from his belongings.\n",
[202]="70061777\n1\tLhúngobel can be found along the River Lune in the north-western reaches of Yondershire. Erfith has asked you to free his companions that were captured by the goblins at Lhúngobel. Dourhands can be found in the ruins of Lhúngobel.\t\n2\tTalk to Erfith\tErfith can be found on a hill just off the road near the border of Ered Luin in Yondershire. You have successfully freed several of Erfith's kin from the goblins at Lhúngobel. You should talk to Erfith.\n",
[203]="7000732D\n1\tDefeat wights (total: 12)\tWights can be found amongst the mounds and barrows of the Edain, in eastern Haudh Lin. Glamír has asked you to destroy the evil wights of Haudh Lin.\n2\tTalk to Glamír\tGlamír waits in the ruin south of the Grimwater within the woods of Western Haudh Lin. You journeyed to the mounds and barrows of the Edain in Haudh Lin and defeated many wights.\n",
[204]="7003783C\n1\tTalk to Éothain\tÉothain is in Aldburg in the Eastfold. Arcil asked you to speak with Éothain and inform him of the decision, but also to deliver an apology.\n2\tTalk to Arcil\tArcil is in the Mead Hall of Aldburg. Éothain has accepted Arcil's apology and asked you to deliver his response.\n",
[205]="7002D3AD\n1\tSeek Dagfinn in Shemeldurj\tDagfinn went off to explore Shemeldurj, an ancient hall of Moria. You should seek Dagfinn at Shemeldurj to ease Túbi's fretting for his friend.\n2\tSearch piles of debris for any promising relics (total: 6)\tPiles of promising debris can be found around Shemeldurj. You should root through several piles of promising debris to seek ancient treasure.\n3\tTell Dagfinn that Shemeldurj appears to be as empty as it looks\tDagfinn is in Shemeldurj in the north-west of the Great Delving, near Durin's Threshold. You should tell Dagfinn that you found nothing promising anywhere in Shemeldurj.\n4\tReturn to Túbi Thickfist\tTúbi Thickfist is atop the great stair in Durin's Threshold in the west of the Great Delving. You should return to Túbi Thickfist with news of Dagfinn's fruitless search.\n",
[206]="7002D3AF\n1\tFind the Chamber of Deep Thought\tThe Chamber of Deep Thought is east through the tunnel from Durin's Threshold, then south. You should search the Chamber of Deep Thought for any relics of interest.\n2\tExamine the cocoon\tThe cocoon is in the Chamber of Deep Thought in the west of the Great Delving. You should search the cocoon for anything that might be of value to the dwarves.\n3\tReturn to Túbi Thickfist\tTúbi Thickfist is at the top of the stair of Durin's Threshold. You should return to Túbi Thickfist with news of your search.\n",
[207]="70017927\n1\tTalk to Andyri\tAndyri is at Lin Giliath, in Meluinen on the North Downs. You have been told that Andyri of Lin Giliath is seeking Wardens for some task of importance.\n2\tTalk to Andyri and travel to the Stone-troll caves\tAndyri is at Lin Giliath, in Meluinen on the North Downs. The Elf Andyri has asked for your help and is waiting to speak with you.\n3\tTalk to Andyri at Lin Giliath\tAndyri is at Lin Giliath, in Meluinen on the North Downs. You have proven a valuable ally in the darkness of the Stone-troll caves and should speak now with Andyri.\n",
[208]="70020DC5\n1\tCollect marigolds (total: 10)\tMarigolds can be found throughout the Gloomglens. Violed Isbrun has asked you to gather marigolds for her. She uses the flowers to defend her garden against small pests.\n2\tVioled Isbrun's garden is in Maur Tulhau. You should bring the marigolds you collected back to Violed's garden and plant them.\t\n3\tTalk to Violed Isbrun at Maur Tulhau\tVioled Isbrun is in Maur Tulhau. You should speak with Violed Isbrun again and let her know that you have done as she asked.\n",
[209]="7006B772\n1\tDestroy powder-laden waggons (total: 4)\tThe Ordâkhai waggons in Eshadûr, south of the Ikorbân River, must be destroyed to protect Dumûri control of the Wrackwade.\n2\tTalk to Ningêna at the Wrackwade\tYou have successfully destroyed the Ordâkhai powder-laden waggons in Eshadûr. You should now travel to the Wrackwade and talk to Ningêna, the Dumûri captain. The Wrackwade is a river crossing east of Iridír.\n",
[210]="7006692F\n1\tPick up the stack of planks in Iáphel\tMiruhir has asked you to move recovered flotsam from where it is stacked by the fence to Tregeth, who waits in town. Collect recovered flotsam.\n2\tTalk to Tregeth\t\n",
[211]="7005A56C\n1\tTalk to Lúka\t\n",
[212]="70052B18\n1\tTalk to Atta\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. Ríkmar has told you to speak to a Woodman named Atta, the eldest man in Hultvís, who has refused to leave the settlement since the days of his youth.\n2\tTalk to Atta and complete 'Skulking the Wood'\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. Long met with derision and pity by his own people, Atta has refused to speak of what troubles him for many years. Perhaps if you aid him and earn his trust, he will be more willing to share his tale.\n3\tTalk to Atta\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. You have helped Atta by laying traps in the woods outside Hultvís. You should return to Atta and see if he is more willing to speak of what troubles him.\n4\tTalk to Atta and complete 'Old and Mad'\030Talk to Atta and complete 'Spirits of the Taken'\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. Atta has told you of a terrible creature that once haunted the vales, but he dares not to speak its true name. You should aid him with another task and speak to the children of Hultvís to learn more of the creature called Ubb.\n5\tTalk to Atta\tAtta can be found in Hultvís. You have learned more of Ubb from the children of Hultvís, and you have banished a number of sorrowful spirits in Avabárg. You should return to Atta.\n",
[213]="70065DBD\n1\tTalk to Cúdor\tThe defender at Minlos beacon has asked you to speak to Cúdor in Tumladen. Cúdor can be found at Tumladen to the west of Minlos beacon.\n2\tDefeat Grafeleg bears (total: 8)\030Defeat Grafeleg fugitives (total: 6)\030Defeat a Grafeleg matron (quantity: see journal)\030Defeat Zagrazg\tCúdor has informed you of an Orc party which has begun to corrupt the bears of Grafeleg. Grafeleg can be found north of Tumladen.\n3\tTalk to Cúdor\tYou should tell Cúdor that the threat in Grafeleg has been addressed. Cúdor can be found in Tumladen.\n",
[214]="700173D7\n1\tBring the husk to Narfi in the Twenty-first Hall\030Collect Desiccated Husk\tNarfi is at the Twenty-first Hall. You discovered that Igash was something more than a typical Orc and are looking for some answers to newfound questions.\n2\tTalk to Pálmar at Anazârmekhem\tPálmar is at Anazârmekhem. Narfi could give you very little information about the strange husk, but he thought that his agent, Pálmar -- posted in Anazármekhem -- may know something about the strange fire behind Igash's eyes.\n",
[215]="7002EEFF\n1\tTalk to Agela\t\n2\tTalk to Agela\tAgela is hiding within the ruins of Thornhope. You should escort Agela to safety.\n3\tTalk to Agela at Béortnoth's camp\tAgela is at Béortnoth's camp, outside of Thornhope. You should speak with Agela when you return to Béortnoth's camp.\n",
[216]="70061797\n1\tFind the captured Bounder in Taerhad\tA captured Bounder can be found somewhere in Taerhad. In the hopes that it will draw out Sharkey's lieutenant, Mal Ragwood has asked you to free a captured Bounder from the half-orcs at Taerhad.\n2\tFree the captured Bounder at Taerhad Defeat Sharkey's Lieutenant\tThe captured Bounder can be found atop Taerhad in Yondershire. You have found the captured Bounder at Taerhad. You should attempt to free him and also keep watch for any sign of Sharkey's lieutenant.\n3\tTalk to Bounder Hawkwort at Taerhad\tBounder Hawkwort can be found at Taerhad in Yondershire. You have defeated Sharkey's lieutenant. You should talk to Bounder Hawkwort and aid in freeing him from the half-orcs at Taerhad.\n4\tTalk to Bounder Hawkwort in the Roaring Bull\tBounder Hawkwort can be found inside the Roaring Bull in Long Cleeve in Yondershire. After freeing Bounder Hawkwort from the half-orcs at Taerhad, he has asked you to meet him at the Roaring Bull. You should talk to Bounder Hawkwort.\n",
[217]="70067160\n1\tTalk to Yared\tYared stands by the stacks of crates in north-western Furukzahar.\n2\tSearch crates of tools until you find the rock-scrapers\tThe rock-scrapers demanded by Shegai will be in one of the crates of tools near Yared in Furukzahar.\n3\tTalk to Yared\tYared is by the crates of tools in north-western Furukzahar.\n",
[218]="7002F98C\n1\tSpeak to Sahard about the strange creatures\tSahard resides at his farm just east of the Faldham mead hall. Nothwulf believes that Sahard, an elder of Faldham, may be able to shed light on the reports of mysterious beasts seen to the east.\n2\tSpeak to Sahard\tSahard resides at his farm just east of the Faldham mead hall. Sahard wishes to discuss his plan with you.\n3\tLure láthbears with bait and defeat any that appear (total: 3)\tThe láthbears seem to reside among the trees to the east of Sahard's farm. Sahard has given you food to be used as bait for luring out láthbears, so that you might take a closer look.\n4\tSpeak to Inhere at the northern edge of the trees\tInhere has been watching the láthbears at the northern edge of the woods. Sahard has asked you to seek out the Rohirrim, Inhere, to see what he may have discovered.\n",
[219]="70047BA1\n1\tCollect hauntreek (total: 10)\tHauntreek can be found in the ruins of Nuiharn, north-west of Haerondir. Collect hauntreek for Rhadrog.\n2\tBurn hauntreek in braziers (total: 10)\tBurn the hauntreek you collected in the braziers found around Haerondir. The hauntreek will cause the fire to burn a strange blue colour.\n3\tSpeak with Rhadrog\tRhadrog can be found in Haerondir. You should speak with Rhadrog.\n",
[220]="700216DA\n1\tCollect fake Dorwinion White from Sogadan in Rivendell\tSogadan the Vintner is in Rivendell, away in the Trollshaws. You should collect Dorwinion Red wine from Sogadan, but it shall be delivered as Dorwinion White upon being served to Lendasil.\n2\tBring the fake Dorwinion White to Lendasil in Edhelion\tLendasil is in the Ruins of Edhelion in Ered Luin, waiting to taste the Dorwinion White. You have only false wine to give Lendasil... red wine, actually. You should bring it to her at once.\n",
[221]="700687C8\n1\tRetrieve waterlogged crates from the waters of Sail-haven (total: 12)\tWaterlogged crates can be found in the canals and in the harbour surrounding the Rovers' Yard in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. Galyat has asked you to retrieve waterlogged crates that have sunken into the canals and harbour of the Sail-haven.\n2\tDeliver the waterlogged crates to Galyat\tGalyat can be found near the Rovers' Yard to the east of the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You have retrieved a number of waterlogged crates from the canals and harbour of the Sail-haven in Umbar Baharbêl. You should deliver them to Galyat.\n",
[222]="70040EE0\n1\tDestroy barrels of ale on Corsair ships (total: 6)\tBarrels of ale can be found on the three Corsair ships moored at Edhellond. Dolvir has asked you to burn barrels of ale in hopes of shattering the morale of the Corsairs.\n2\tTalk to Dolvir\tDolvir can be found on a hilltop to the east of Edhellond. You have destroyed a huge supply of Corsair ale, and should return to Dolvir with news of your success.\n",
[223]="7006F326\n1\tMeet with Ulishár at the cross-road south-west of Gadim-ûn\tUlishár suggested that the two of you meet up at the cross-road south-west of Gadim-ûn.\n2\tTalk to Ulishár at the cross-road south-west of Gadim-ûn\tUlishár stands beside the road, gazing eastward.\n3\tDefeat brigands at Zakhûr ([see journal]/5)\tUlishár spotted a camp of brigands to the east, and he believes you should oppose their plans before you continue westward.\n4\tDefeat brigands at Zakhûr (4/5)\tUlishár spotted a camp of brigands to the east, and he believes you should oppose their plans before you continue westward.\n5\tTalk to Ulishár outside Zakhûr\tUlishár has prevented a brigand from escaping Zakhûr: a brigand with a familiar face.\n6\tTalk to Mashdagâl outside Zakhûr\tMashdagâl is outside Zakhûr.\n7\tPick up Mashdagâl's sword to accept his surrender\tNorth-east of Zakhûr, Mashdagâl has surrendered his sword to you.\n8\tHand the sword to Ulishár\tUlishár has asked for the sword.\n9\tMashdagâl breaks into a run!\tMashdagâl moves suddenly, attempting to escape!\n10\tTalk to Ulishár outside Zakhûr\tUlishár is outside Zakhûr.\n11\tMeet with Ulishár on the eastern bank of the dry Usâl River in An Shêru\tUlishár asked to meet you on the eastern bank of the dry Usâl River in An Shêru.\n12\tTalk to Ulishár on the eastern bank of the dry Usâl River in An Shêru\tUlishár stands by the eastern bank of the dry Usâl River in An Shêru.\n13\tCross to the western bank of the dry Usâl River in An Shêru\tUlishár is ready to meet you on the western bank of the dry Usâl River in An Shêru. He pointed out a place to the north-west where you might climb out of the channel.\n14\tTalk to Ulishár on the western bank of the dry Usâl River in An Shêru\tUlishár stands by the western bank of the dry Usâl River in An Shêru.\n",
[224]="70001203\n1\tGather drake-eggs (total: 5)\tThere are drake nests far to the east of Gabilshathûr in the valley of Dolroth. Kol has asked you to collect drake-eggs to supplement the inedible provender you already provided.\n2\tBring the drake-eggs to Kol\tKol is at Gabilshathûr, far to the east of the drake-nests. You have counted a fair number of drake-nests and should now return to Kol with the information you have gathered.\n",
})
